---
/**
 * The homepage. Nine body sections became four.
 *
 * Measured at 1440x900 and 390x844 against a built site, scrolled to the
 * bottom and settled first, the page was 7,585px / 14,338px for 658 words:
 * mostly pictures and padding, at 1.8x claude.com and 2.4x anthropic.com. It
 * made ONE argument four times, in `sp-why-now`, `sp-not-a-slice`,
 * `home-difference` and `metrics-bar`, and it shipped two chip strips of the
 * same idea 3,400px apart.
 *
 * What left and why:
 *   - `SPHero` -> `SPHomeHero`. The shared hero is pinned to
 *     `min-height: 100dvh` for 25 other pages, so nothing real ever cleared
 *     the fold here. See that file for the rest.
 *   - `sp-why-now` moved to its own route, `/[lang]/why-now`. Neither
 *     reference homepage carries an equivalent.
 *   - `logo-wall` deleted. It was strictly subsumed by `integrations-strip`:
 *     every one of its six categories has a concrete instance among the other
 *     strip's fifteen chips, and it sat 3,400px earlier with no heading of its
 *     own, reading as a page-break artifact.
 *   - `metrics-bar` deleted. All four of its numbers were already prose in
 *     `home-difference` 2,200px above it, and one of them ("241 GB in under
 *     60 seconds") flatly contradicted the hero's "3.2 TB in 4.7s".
 *   - `sp-not-a-slice` deleted, with its `SPHomeNotASlice.astro` component and
 *     its 12-leaf `notASlice.*` i18n namespace. It argued the same point as
 *     `home-difference` ("partial tools copy one piece, we copy all of it"),
 *     which was the LAST surviving pair of the "ONE argument four times"
 *     problem named at the top of this note. `home-difference` states it
 *     better: four before/after pairs against four bordered cards plus a
 *     winner card whose description repeated the after-points verbatim.
 *   - `pricing-preview` deleted, with its `PricingPreview.astro` component and
 *     its 3-leaf `pricingPreview.*` i18n namespace. It was a second copy of
 *     `/[lang]/pricing`: the same `buildPlans()` cards, the same billing
 *     toggle, the same tax note, ending in a "compare all plans" link to the
 *     real page. The header nav links `/[lang]/pricing` directly, so the
 *     route was never reachable only through here. The three `#pricing`
 *     fragment links that pointed at this section (footer, refund policy, the
 *     `ceo` persona CTA) now point at `/[lang]/pricing` itself.
 *
 * The five 12-line `SPHome*` pass-through wrappers are gone with them. They
 * forwarded `lang` and nothing else, and one of them renamed `HomeDifference`
 * to `SPHomeBeforeAfter`, so the section had four names for one thing.
 *
 * What arrived since: the SOLUTION CONSTELLATION, at position 1 under the hero.
 * The `/[lang]/solutions` index existed to hold exactly this figure and nothing
 * else, so it was a click between the homepage and the only map of the 21
 * pages. It carries `id="solutions"`, which is the target the header, the
 * drawer, the footer and the 404 page now link to, and the fragment ids inside
 * it (`#copy`, `#test`, `#recover`, `#platform`) are the ones the compact
 * constellation on 24 other pages points at.
 */
import type { Language } from '../../i18n/types';
import { createTranslator } from '../../i18n/utils';
import SPHomeHero from './SPHomeHero.astro';
import SPHomeVideo from './SPHomeVideo.astro';
import SolutionConstellation from './SolutionConstellation.astro';
import HomeDifference from '../HomeDifference.astro';
import SPHomeBottomCta from './SPHomeBottomCta.astro';

interface Props {
  lang: Language;
}

const { lang } = Astro.props as Props;
const { t } = createTranslator(lang);
---

<div class="sp-page">
  <SPHomeHero lang={lang} />
  {/* THE CONSTELLATION LEADS, and it is the `full` one, not a compact variant.
      Decision L9.4 called for "the compact 4-node variant ... dropped into the
      hero slot L5 vacates". Built and measured, that does not work: the compact
      GEOMETRY is a 1440x580 ellipse whose arms are sized to hold ONE role's
      siblings clustered together (constellation.ts GEOMETRY.compact; the
      solution pages feed it slugsForRole()). Four nodes, one per role, land at
      the far reach of four different arms, so the figure rendered 1265x510 with
      its labels flung to the corners and an empty middle. Screenshotted before
      this note was written.

      The OUTCOME L9.4 wanted -- the page opens on the one figure only this
      product can show, instead of on a baked video poster whose big-number
      treatment is the generic default and which cannot follow the theme -- is
      delivered by moving the FULL figure above the video. It keeps its heading,
      its #solutions id (linked from the header, drawer, footer, 404 and 24
      pages) and its role anchors. No CTA is added, so L5 and n6 hold.

      `heading` is what makes this render an <h2> and take the .cx--boxed frame.
      Without it the `full` preset emits no heading at all, and the homepage's
      one <h1> is SPHomeHero's, so a second one here would be wrong anyway. */}
  <SolutionConstellation lang={lang} id="solutions" preset="full" heading={t('solutions.title')} />
  <SPHomeVideo lang={lang} />
  <HomeDifference lang={lang} />
  <SPHomeBottomCta lang={lang} />
</div>

{/* The homepage video mounts through the shared hydrator rather than as an island,
    because `plyr` reads `document` at module scope and cannot be server-rendered.
    Same script SolutionPage.astro loads for its own hero video. */}
<script src="../../scripts/tutorial-video-hydrate.ts"></script>
